#. ~ Practice name
#: data/json/recipes/practice/fabrication.json
msgid "redsmithing (beginner)"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of practice "redsmithing (beginner)"
#: data/json/recipes/practice/fabrication.json
msgid ""
"Practice the basics of redsmithing by working copper into some simple forms "
"and designs."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Practice name
#: data/json/recipes/practice/fabrication.json
msgid "redsmithing (advanced)"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of practice "redsmithing (advanced)"
#: data/json/recipes/practice/fabrication.json
msgid ""
"Practice the more advanced techniques of redsmithing by working bronze into "
"different and complex forms and designs."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Practice name
#: data/json/recipes/practice/fabrication.json
msgid "blacksmithing"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of practice "blacksmithing"
#: data/json/recipes/practice/fabrication.json
msgid "Practice working metal into some simple but useful forms and designs."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Practice name
#: data/json/recipes/practice/fabrication.json
msgid "armorsmithing"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of practice "armorsmithing"
#: data/json/recipes/practice/fabrication.json
msgid ""
"Practice working metal into the form of various armor pieces, and test their "
"articulation with you using some cotton for padding along with the armor "
"pieces."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Practice name
#: data/json/recipes/practice/fabrication.json
msgid "bladesmithing"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of practice "bladesmithing"
#: data/json/recipes/practice/fabrication.json
msgid ""
"Practice working metal into the form of useful blades of all sizes and "
"designs, grind them until you learn how much is too much."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Practice name
#: data/json/recipes/practice/fabrication.json
msgid "manual tooling"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of practice "manual tooling"
#: data/json/recipes/practice/fabrication.json
msgid ""
"Practice working metal into the complex forms and designs of several tools "
"like hammers and screwdrivers."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Practice name
#: data/json/recipes/practice/fabrication.json
msgid "case hardening"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of practice "case hardening"
#: data/json/recipes/practice/fabrication.json
msgid ""
"Practice heating steel packed in charcoal at different high temperatures and "
"times, and then comparing the properties of the resulting hard case."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Practice name
#: data/json/recipes/practice/fabrication.json
msgid "quenching & tempering"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of practice "quenching & tempering"
#: data/json/recipes/practice/fabrication.json
msgid ""
"Practice heating chunks of steel and quickly cooling them down with water, "
"and then, to reduce brittleness and restore ductility, heating them again to "
"maximize its properties."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of practice "melee (beginner)"
#: data/json/recipes/practice/melee.json
msgid ""
"Swing around a weapon-shaped object to try and get a feel for what fighting "
"might be like.  It's difficult without any instruction to guide you, but "
"hopefully this practice will help you to swing at your enemies without "
"falling on your face or panicking too much."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of practice "melee (intermediate)"
#: data/json/recipes/practice/melee.json
msgid ""
"Practice the basics of combat with the guidance of a manual or prior "
"knowledge.  Even without a sparring partner you can practice your footwork, "
"form, and flow drills to help avoid overswinging and stumbling."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of practice "cutting (beginner)"
#: data/json/recipes/practice/melee.json
msgid ""
"Practice some of the basics of combat with cutting weapons, such as how to "
"keep your edge lined up and how to not chop your own leg off."
msgstr ""
